## Verification by task type

Classify the task **before** editing. `breaking: true` always means full.

| `type`                                  | Level    | Reviewer               |
| --------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------- |
| `feat`, `refactor`                      | **full** | yes, at activity close |
| `fix`, `perf`, `test`                   | medium   | no                     |
| `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `ci`, `build` | light    | no                     |

| Level  | Command                                     | What runs                                                |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| light  | `node scripts/harness.mjs --for-task <ref>` | changed format/lint + structure/docs + harness self-test |
| medium | same                                        | + affected type check + targeted specs                   |
| full   | same                                        | all gates (final gate at activity close)                 |

- `node scripts/harness.mjs --explain <ref>` prints the level and the gate set
  without running anything.
- `node scripts/harness.mjs --fast` is for iteration;
  `node scripts/harness.mjs --changed` derives light/medium from the working
  tree.
- Each task runs **its own level**. The reviewer is invoked **once at activity
  close**, only when the activity level is full.
- A `feat` needs a new or extended spec. A non-breaking `fix` needs a
  regression test that fails without the fix. The reviewer rejects otherwise.
- Full harness: `node scripts/harness.mjs` (or `npm run harness`).
- Full matrix, docs/tests per type and pending optimizations:
  `docs/harness/verification.md`.

### Hard rules

- Never run the full gate after every edit; use `--fast` between edits and the
  task level when the task is done.
- Maximum **2 full runs per activity**. A third run needs a concrete reason
  (e.g. a release/PR gate).
- Do not edit files while the harness is running.
- The reviewer sees the whole activity, not a partial change.
- Historical activities are not migrated; `task.type ?? activity.type ??
'medium'` is the fallback.
